[2026-03-15T23:26:33.688Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YRTQ8tVV4kFm48sz6rpGCQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The telemetry module is OpenTelemetry! That's the module that's trying to connect to `127.0.0.1:44863` - it's trying to send telemetry data to a collector that doesn't exist. This is the `___netlify-telemetry.mjs` file.\n\nThe error `connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:44863` is from the OpenTelemetry collector trying to report telemetry. But wait - the error message says \"Function debug has returned an error\", meaning the function's response is the error. So the telemetry error is being treated as the function's error.\n \nActually, I'm realizing the real issue here - the netlify dev bootstrap is trying to send telemetry and failing, but that shouldn't be blocking the function execution itself. Let me reconsider whether the `--offline` flag is actually preventing the telemetry connection properly, or if I need to disable telemetry entirely. But wait, I'm noticing something else - all the tests were failing with \"element not found\" for image-gallery, which suggests the problem might be deeper than just the telemetry connection issue.\n\nLooking back at the commit history, image-gallery tests were passing before, so something in the environment must have changed. I should check if the netlify dev version got updated or if something got corrupted in the setup.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1140,"cache_read_input_tokens":110931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1140,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d86e976-1032-4e20-b927-fb9bc4791925","uuid":"0c97aebc-70af-494c-923c-d4e89ec877d1"}
